cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this archive, please cite it and the article it accompanies."
type: software
title: "KeepCount: conditions, code, records and history"
abstract: >-
  The conditions, code, records, notes and git history of an audit of what images of behavioral data keep, applied to
  a transform that turns keystroke times into shaded tiles, one per sentence, through speed and rest. Every
  computation ran a script on conditions committed before the script was first run. The keystroke data are not
  redistributed. The code (src/, works/*.py, tools/, tests/) is under the MIT License (LICENSE); the documents,
  conditions, records, texts and images are under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (LICENSE-docs).
